      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Mitosis is the process where a single cell divides into two identical daughter cells. This essential process allows for growth and repair in living organisms by producing exact copies of the original cell. Throughout this division, the cell faithfully duplicates its DNA so that each new cell receives a complete and identical set of genetic instructions. Understanding this cycle helps us learn how living things maintain themselves and develop.",
